(1676076, 226905, 36499, '<td valign="top">returning to comment: please dont take offense to this as my only intention is to help( read my profile for additional info): for me this photo would be alot better if the cat was in sharp focus rather than the tree branches. if you are using photoshop 7( which is what i use) this is how i would adjust it. slight boost of contrast then i would slightly boost color saturations(master) then go to selective color and in the lue setting i would boost the cyan levels. red i would boost the magenta and yellow levels. this is just my best guess to get the most out of this photo. i hope i have helped you as that is my only intention.  I do love the composistion of this photo.good luck and i hope to see you at the top soon.</td>', 'returning to comment: please dont take offense to this as my only intention is to help( read my profile for additional info): for me this photo would be alot better if the cat was in sharp focus rather than the tree branches. if you are using photoshop 7( which is what i use) this is how i would adjust it. slight boost of contrast then i would slightly boost color saturations(master) then go to selective color and in the lue setting i would boost the cyan levels. red i would boost the magenta and yellow levels. this is just my best guess to get the most out of this photo. i hope i have helped you as that is my only intention.  I do love the composistion of this photo.good luck and i hope to see you at the top soon.', '2005-09-05 14:13:14.000000', NULL, 1),
