(1698311, 225858, 30049, '<td valign="top">Reworked after monitor calibration (crop is different):<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=230073" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30049/thumb/230073.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30049/thumb/230073.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30049/thumb/230073.jpg"/></a><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-09-12 08:56:28.</i></td>', 'Reworked after monitor calibration (crop is different):', '2005-09-12 09:54:22.000000', '2005-09-12 09:56:28.000000', 0),
(1698319, 225426, 34192, '<td valign="top">Amazingly underrated image.  I had this in my top 3.</td>', 'Amazingly underrated image.  I had this in my top 3.', '2005-09-12 09:57:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(1698326, 226589, 42871, '<td valign="top">I am very pleased with the performance of my first challenge. I agree with the comments that the rear part of the horse was to dark. I blurred the background in Photoshop. In reality the sculpture is about 5-10 feet from the building and there was no angle where it didnt appear in the shot. I felt that it was to distracting so I made the creative choice to blur it and keep the focus on the man and the horse. But I should have waited for better light, lesson learned :)<br/> <br/>I drive by this on the way home from work every day and I knew it would be a good subject for the challenge. I even had a picture of the way I wanted it to look in my head. In the end, other than what was already mentioned, it came out exactly as I had imagined it. Which is what photography is all about! So I am very pleased. Thanks all.</td>', 'I am very pleased with the performance of my first challenge. I agree with the comments that the rear part of the horse was to dark. I blurred the background in Photoshop. In reality the sculpture is about 5-10 feet from the building and there was no angle where it didnt appear in the shot. I felt that it was to distracting so I made the creative choice to blur it and keep the focus on the man and the horse. But I should have waited for better light, lesson learned :) I drive by this on the way home from work every day and I knew it would be a good subject for the challenge. I even had a picture of the way I wanted it to look in my head. In the end, other than what was already mentioned, it came out exactly as I had imagined it. Which is what photography is all about! So I am very pleased. Thanks all.', '2005-09-12 09:59:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(1698333, 226675, 25355, '<td valign="top">They still have those installations? I got some good (slide) shots back in 1984 at the Barbican Centre, though it was a much lower and more tunnelled affair. But great image, and the person really adds to the atmsophere of this strange world of colour. Congratulations on your high placing.</td>', 'They still have those installations? I got some good (slide) shots back in 1984 at the Barbican Centre, though it was a much lower and more tunnelled affair. But great image, and the person really adds to the atmsophere of this strange world of colour. Congratulations on your high placing.', '2005-09-12 10:01:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(1698339, 226791, 11897, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ttreit:</b></div><hr/><i> The fur on the right is blown out which is unfortunate, because otherwise it''s a pretty nice shot. I might have tried to clean his eyes up a little bit more. My eye is immediately drawn to his left eye (right as we look at the shot) and I wish it wasn''t goopy in the corner. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thanks for your comment, I would point out though the " blown " effect on the fur was intentional.</td>', 'Originally posted by ttreit: The fur on the right is blown out which is unfortunate, because otherwise it''s a pretty nice shot. I might have tried to clean his eyes up a little bit more. My eye is immediately drawn to his left eye (right as we look at the shot) and I wish it wasn''t goopy in the corner.  Thanks for your comment, I would point out though the " blown " effect on the fur was intentional.', '2005-09-12 10:02:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(1698359, 226814, 37005, '<td valign="top">This plant is an allium gone to seed.  I loved the texture of this plant and couldn''t wait to get my hands on photographing it!</td>', 'This plant is an allium gone to seed.  I loved the texture of this plant and couldn''t wait to get my hands on photographing it!', '2005-09-12 10:07:57.000000', NULL, 0),
