(1700198, 226372, 17507, '<td valign="top">wow, I have no idea why people missed the link to the challenge! I gave this a 7, and I don''t hand out votes above 6 very often at all! I thought your inclusion of red, blue, green, and yellow was wonderful, and I thought that (despite the small size and fairly soft focus) people would recognize the merit of this picture. I can''t believe all the 4''s! Gah! It''s a good picture anyway :)</td>', 'wow, I have no idea why people missed the link to the challenge! I gave this a 7, and I don''t hand out votes above 6 very often at all! I thought your inclusion of red, blue, green, and yellow was wonderful, and I thought that (despite the small size and fairly soft focus) people would recognize the merit of this picture. I can''t believe all the 4''s! Gah! It''s a good picture anyway :)', '2005-09-12 17:21:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(1700218, 224736, 25397, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bear_music:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by legalbeagle:</b></div><hr/><i> Bad luck Robt - your image was very impressive.  The colours are sublime (I must admit, I see the colour contrast rather more than any than luminosity contrast).  <br/> <br/>Keep that 20D charged in future (how did the date get reset?  My backup battery seems to keep forever). </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It was never properly set to begin with; it was 12 hours off. Dumb error. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I still love ya</td>', 'Originally posted by bear_music: Originally posted by legalbeagle: Bad luck Robt - your image was very impressive.  The colours are sublime (I must admit, I see the colour contrast rather more than any than luminosity contrast).   Keep that 20D charged in future (how did the date get reset?  My backup battery seems to keep forever).   It was never properly set to begin with; it was 12 hours off. Dumb error.  I still love ya', '2005-09-12 17:26:31.000000', NULL, 0),
