(1701094, 226676, 18080, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by BradP:</b></div><hr/><i> Guess I have to go against the majority here on this one Manny.<br/>Composition and subject is, as always, first-rate.<br/>In this instance, I don''t feel the processing was in your normal high standards.<br/>Too harsh in many ways, especially around the flowers, and a bit odd around her right upper arm (focus/clarity?).<br/>Did you consider a softer finish on the flowers by chance? A bit of gaussion blur?<br/>Just personal preference/opinion.<br/> <br/>Congrats on the Magazine shots by the way. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Have to dissagree here. I think this is the best shot you have taken, and one of the greatest shots on this site. But that is just my opinion. And to me that is the most important opinion.<br/>Well done<br/>I Love it</td>', 'Originally posted by BradP: Guess I have to go against the majority here on this one Manny.Composition and subject is, as always, first-rate.In this instance, I don''t feel the processing was in your normal high standards.Too harsh in many ways, especially around the flowers, and a bit odd around her right upper arm (focus/clarity?).Did you consider a softer finish on the flowers by chance? A bit of gaussion blur?Just personal preference/opinion. Congrats on the Magazine shots by the way.   Have to dissagree here. I think this is the best shot you have taken, and one of the greatest shots on this site. But that is just my opinion. And to me that is the most important opinion.Well doneI Love it', '2005-09-12 21:14:06.000000', NULL, 0),
